 "review": {"identity": "swe2-max-1", "method": "The split's integration step reviewed the whole prefix locally with `retail,gpu,audio` (CS_GAME_DIR, CS_ENGINE_IMAGE): `cargo test --locked -p cs_app -p cs_formats -- accept_parity4_lens_flare_ --include-ignored` ran this task's own draw-path tests (the MissionLensFlarePlugin over a stand-in scene camera and a bound node-3237 object), the retail legs through the production readers (the `sun` node's stored flagged light and `lflare1..4` out of C3) and the ignored windowed test, which drove the owner's own command `cs --cs-path $CS_GAME_DIR --mission M01 --smoke-seconds 45 --capture-dir private/evidence/PARITY4-LENS-FLARE` on this machine's GPU (Apple M3 Pro, Metal). The smoke's sun-aim phase froze the flight on the `Menu` hold — never the `PlayerRequest` hold that would raise the Esc map over the frame — wrote a test placement that put the camera-anchored `sun` node's stored bulb on the designed frame fraction of the owner's reference capture (comparison-only, never committed), measured the live camera's projected position and corrected once, then photographed `lens_flare` and `lens_flare_hidden` — the same frozen frame with only the four `lflare` quads hidden — and counted the pixels each quad added. The run wrote both framebuffer PNGs and report.json, which this report hashes as artifacts. The run is automated, never `human_play`, and no original executable ran; the aim, the fraction and the hidden-frame comparison are designed, not verified_original. This harness derives every field from the recorded log, production discovery of $CS_GAME_DIR, the smoke's report and the hashes of those artifacts. Validated with tools/validate_evidence.py --require-pass."},
